WEBVTT

00:00.720 --> 00:01.600
Mark 11

00:01.600 --> 00:07.620
Now when they drew near to Jerusalem, to Bethphage and Bethany, at the Mount of Olives,

00:08.140 --> 00:10.840
Jesus sent two of his disciples and said to them,

00:11.540 --> 00:16.180
Go into the village in front of you, and immediately as you enter it you will find a colt tied,

00:16.420 --> 00:19.580
on which no one has ever sat. Untie it and bring it.

00:20.380 --> 00:22.780
If anyone says to you, Why are you doing this?

00:23.140 --> 00:26.360
Say, The Lord has need of it, and will send it back here immediately.

00:26.360 --> 00:32.140
And they went away and found a colt tied at a door outside in the street, and they untied it.

00:32.460 --> 00:34.500
And some of those standing there said to them,

00:35.160 --> 00:36.960
What are you doing untying the colt?

00:37.280 --> 00:40.840
And they told them what Jesus had said, and they let them go.

00:41.400 --> 00:45.700
And they brought the colt to Jesus and threw their cloaks on it, and he sat on it.

00:46.260 --> 00:51.500
And many spread their cloaks on the road, and others spread leafy branches that they had cut from the fields.

00:52.080 --> 00:54.980
And those who went before and those who followed were shouting,

00:55.700 --> 00:56.300
Hold on!

00:57.180 --> 01:00.980
Blessed is he who comes in the name of the Lord!

01:01.800 --> 01:05.520
Blessed is the coming kingdom of our father David!

01:06.320 --> 01:08.400
Hosanna in the highest!

01:10.380 --> 01:13.260
And he entered Jerusalem and went into the temple.

01:13.700 --> 01:16.760
And when he had looked around at everything as it was already late,

01:17.120 --> 01:18.960
he went out to Bethany with the twelve.

01:20.100 --> 01:23.560
On the following day, when they came from Bethany, he was hungry,

01:23.820 --> 01:26.340
and seeing in the distance a fig tree and leaf,

01:26.620 --> 01:28.920
he went to see if he could find anything on it.

01:29.360 --> 01:33.680
When he came to it, he found nothing but leaves, for it was not the season for figs.

01:33.940 --> 01:35.200
And he said to it,

01:35.880 --> 01:38.600
May no one ever eat fruit from you again.

01:39.380 --> 01:40.880
And his disciples heard it.

01:41.920 --> 01:43.540
And they came to Jerusalem.

01:44.080 --> 01:48.900
And he entered the temple and began to drive out those who sold and those who bought in the temple.

01:49.400 --> 01:53.680
And he overturned the tables of the money changers and the seats of those who sold pigeons.

01:54.540 --> 01:56.340
And he would not allow anyone to come in.

01:56.340 --> 01:57.640
And he would not allow anyone to carry anything through the temple.

01:58.040 --> 02:00.060
And he was teaching them and saying to them,

02:00.720 --> 02:02.500
Oh, is it not written,

02:02.680 --> 02:05.680
My house shall be called a house of prayer for all the nations?

02:06.220 --> 02:09.120
But you have made it a den of robbers.

02:09.600 --> 02:13.940
And the chief priests and the scribes heard it and were seeking a way to destroy him,

02:14.200 --> 02:17.920
for they feared him because all the crowd was astonished at his teaching.

02:18.740 --> 02:21.220
And when evening came, they went out of the city.

02:22.120 --> 02:24.040
As they passed by in the morning,

02:24.040 --> 02:26.180
they saw the fig tree withered away,

02:26.340 --> 02:27.000
to its roots.

02:27.500 --> 02:29.320
And Peter remembered and said to him,

02:30.100 --> 02:31.140
Rabbi, look!

02:31.680 --> 02:34.040
The fig tree that you cursed has withered.

02:34.600 --> 02:36.380
And Jesus answered them,

02:37.120 --> 02:38.340
Have faith in God.

02:38.860 --> 02:39.840
Truly I say to you,

02:39.920 --> 02:41.280
whoever says to this mountain,

02:41.620 --> 02:43.360
Be taken up and thrown into the sea,

02:43.680 --> 02:45.300
and does not doubt in his heart,

02:45.460 --> 02:48.040
but believes that what he says will come to pass,

02:48.380 --> 02:50.000
it will be done for him.

02:51.060 --> 02:52.280
Therefore I tell you,

02:52.280 --> 02:53.880
whatever you ask in prayer,

02:54.320 --> 02:55.760
believe that you have received it,

02:55.760 --> 02:57.260
and it will be yours.

02:58.260 --> 02:59.760
And whenever you stand praying,

02:59.760 --> 03:02.460
forgive, if you have anything against anyone,

03:02.460 --> 03:07.260
so that your Father also who is in heaven may forgive you your trespasses.

03:09.260 --> 03:11.260
And they came again to Jerusalem.

03:11.260 --> 03:13.260
And as he was walking in the temple,

03:13.260 --> 03:16.260
the chief priests and the scribes and the elders came to him.

03:16.260 --> 03:17.760
And they said to him,

03:17.760 --> 03:20.260
By what authority are you doing these things,

03:20.260 --> 03:22.760
or who gave you this authority to do them?

03:22.760 --> 03:24.760
Jesus said to them,

03:24.760 --> 03:27.260
I will ask you one question.

03:27.260 --> 03:30.760
Answer me, and I will tell you by what authority I do these things.

03:31.260 --> 03:34.760
Was the baptism of John from heaven or from man?

03:35.260 --> 03:36.260
Answer me.

03:36.760 --> 03:39.260
And they discussed it with one another, saying,

03:39.260 --> 03:41.760
If we say from heaven, he will say,

03:41.760 --> 03:43.760
Why then did you not believe him?

03:43.760 --> 03:46.260
But shall we say from man?

03:46.760 --> 03:48.260
They were afraid of the people,

03:48.260 --> 03:50.760
for they all held that John really was a prophet.

03:50.760 --> 03:52.760
So they answered Jesus,

03:52.760 --> 03:54.260
We do not know.

03:54.760 --> 03:56.760
And Jesus said to them,

03:56.760 --> 04:00.760
Neither will I tell you by what authority I do these things.

